      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Contract Release",
          "heading": "Joji Nasova stays with Fijian Drua as Newcastle transfer is cancelled",
          "body": "Fijian wing Joji Nasova will remain with the Fijian Drua after his planned transfer to Premiership side Newcastle Red Bulls was cancelled. The 25-year-old Olympic silver medallist had agreed to join the English club, but he has been released from his contract due to undisclosed personal reasons. Newcastle general manager Neil McIlroy confirmed the decision, stating: \"While we were very much looking forward to welcoming Joji to Newcastle Red Bulls, we fully understand and respect the unique personal circumstances that have led to this decision.\""
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Dressing Room",
          "heading": "Ellis Genge delivers expletive-laden speech as footage reveals England dressing room details",
          "body": "Newly released footage from the O2 Inside Line series has captured vice-captain Ellis Genge delivering a fiery, expletive-laden pre-match address before the recent victory in Santiago del Estero. Genge urged his teammates to 'cause some pain' following the football team’s World Cup semi-final exit, a motivation that preceded a chaotic encounter featuring four overlapping England yellow cards. Despite the disciplinary lapses, the squad survived a frantic final TMO decision to secure a 31-24 win, leaving Steve Borthwick’s side fourth in the Nations Championship standings."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Santiago del Estero",
        "referee": "Angus Gardner"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Strategic evolution",
          "heading": "Fabien Galthié abandons traditional positions for a new skill-set fusion",
          "body": "France is moving away from rigid positional definitions in favour of a skill-set fusion, according to recent analysis of the world's top three sides. Alongside South Africa and New Zealand, Les Bleus are prioritising player versatility over traditional jersey numbers, which Fabien Galthié now treats as an administrative convenience rather than a job specification. By selecting combinations of skills tailored to the specific requirements of a test match, the coaching staff aims to create a more dynamic and adaptable team framework."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching scrutiny",
          "heading": "Matt Williams slams Ireland as failing to meet elite test standards",
          "body": "Former coach Matt Williams has labelled Ireland's recent Nations Championship performances as \"well below elite standards,\" following the team's error-strewn 40-21 defeat to New Zealand. Williams criticised the side for a lack of defensive intensity and technical accuracy throughout the July window, pointing to 18 turnovers and 35 missed tackles in the final fixture at Eden Park. Head coach Andy Farrell acknowledged the team's shortcomings, stating, \"Inaccurate is the word,\" while promising a period of reassessment after a difficult campaign."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Historical Context",
          "heading": "Italy Record Rankings Throughout The Nation's Participation In Men's Rugby",
          "body": "Italy has reached a peak of No. 8 in the World Rugby rankings during two distinct windows in their history. The side first achieved this position in 2007, marking a high point for the nation during that year’s international cycle. The Azzurri subsequently returned to the No. 8 spot in 2024. These two periods represent the highest world ranking the team has achieved since the current iteration of the official classification system was established."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching acclaim",
          "heading": "Gregor Townsend earns high praise for Scotland’s impressive international progression",
          "body": "Following the conclusion of the tournament’s Southern Series, Gregor Townsend has received significant recognition for steering Scotland to a successful period of growth. While a statement victory against a tier-one southern giant remains the ultimate objective, the head coach has been lauded for his side’s resilience. Scotland’s ability to compete at altitude against South Africa, alongside recent wins over England and France, highlights a squad momentum that has firmly established them as a consistent, top-tier international threat."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tactical Insight",
          "heading": "Dan Biggar Analyses The Springboks' Superiority Following Wales' Recent Heavy Loss",
          "body": "Following the difficult 43-0 defeat to South Africa in Durban, former Wales fly-half Dan Biggar has highlighted the immense challenge posed by the world champions. Reflecting on the Springboks’ current trajectory, Biggar identifies their suffocating line speed and defensive pressure as the primary hurdles for any opponent. As Wales looks to recalibrate after a challenging start to the Nations Championship, the stark reality of the gap in quality remains the central talking point for supporters and analysts alike."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Disciplinary fallout",
          "heading": "Nigel Owens criticises Tomás Albornoz following misconduct charges after England match",
          "body": "Former referee Nigel Owens has condemned the conduct of Tomás Albornoz and Pumas supporters following the narrow loss to England. Albornoz faces misconduct charges from World Rugby after remonstrating with official Angus Gardner at the final whistle. Owens labelled the player's behaviour and the subsequent abuse directed at match officials as \"totally, totally unacceptable,\" insisting that such actions have no place in the sport. The incident followed a controversial TMO decision that denied Argentina a potential match-tying try."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection News",
          "heading": "Les Kiss Recalls Lukhan Salakaia-Loto in First Wallabies Coaching Selection",
          "body": "New head coach Les Kiss has signalled a fresh start by recalling powerhouse Lukhan Salakaia-Loto in his first 34-man squad. Following a \"robust conversation\" with his coaching staff, Kiss emphasised that no positions are guaranteed as he begins preparations for next month’s Japan series. While the squad retains captain Harry Wilson and core talent, veteran prop James Slipper has been rested, with Isaac Henry serving as the only uncapped player following an injury to Len Ikitau."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Series Preview",
          "heading": "Les Kiss Names Australia Squad for Upcoming Test Series Against Japan",
          "body": "New Australia head coach Les Kiss has announced a 34-man squad for the upcoming two-test series against Japan. The group includes uncapped Reds centre Isaac Henry, who earned selection following an ankle injury to Len Ikitau. Japan enters this series looking to regain form, having recorded two wins and three losses in their last five matches. The team is currently on a run of two straight defeats, including a 42-15 loss to France in their most recent outing."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "edition": "Sunday 26 July",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Transfer news",
          "heading": "Ma’a Nonu signs short-term deal with the Sharks in South Africa",
          "body": "All Blacks legend Ma’a Nonu is set to continue his career in Durban after confirming a short-term move to the Sharks. The 44-year-old double World Cup winner joins the franchise following a successful tenure at RC Toulon. Sources indicate the veteran midfielder will focus on a mentorship role, specifically tasked with guiding young centres Jurenzo Julius and Ethan Hooker. Nonu’s arrival is expected to bolster the club's leadership and culture as part of their ongoing high-performance restructuring."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "467": {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
