      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tactical evolution",
          "heading": "Rassie Erasmus and Springboks prioritise skill-set fusion over traditional positions",
          "body": "South Africa’s recent success in the Nations Championship highlights a shift in selection strategy, where jersey numbers are treated as administrative conveniences rather than rigid job descriptions. Rassie Erasmus is prioritising a fusion of skills—seeking the specific attributes needed for a match rather than filling slots. This approach was evident in the recent international window, where players like Pieter-Steph du Toit seamlessly rotated through multiple roles across three rounds, maintaining high performance levels despite constant tactical adjustments."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
